00:03:13.281 --> 00:03:16.274
why you hear it so much
in the investment world is

00:03:16.274 --> 00:03:17.756
when you're making an investment,

00:03:17.756 --> 00:03:20.254
if you have X amount of
dollars in your savings, right.

00:03:20.254 --> 00:03:24.334
You have $500,000 or $10,000 in savings,

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:26.593
if you put it all into one stock,

00:03:26.593 --> 00:03:27.938
and that stock crashes,

00:03:27.938 --> 00:03:29.368
then you've lost all your money.

00:03:29.368 --> 00:03:31.484
Where if you invest it
into 10 different stocks,

00:03:31.484 --> 00:03:32.829
then one may crash,

00:03:32.829 --> 00:03:34.934
but chances are the other
ones are going to do decently,

00:03:34.934 --> 00:03:37.190
and so overall you've made some money.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.449
You don't know what you're
really doing in investing,

00:03:39.449 --> 00:03:41.402
you're not involved in
any of those companies.

00:03:41.402 --> 00:03:44.486
And so it helps just mitigate the risk.

00:03:44.486 --> 00:03:47.944
Diversifying typically is
a way to minimize your risk

00:03:47.944 --> 00:03:50.490
as opposed to going off
and doing something great.

